Expected behavior: generic, well-researched answer to the user's question — do NOT lean on any of the above.","example_response_self_check":{"score":3,"passed":true,"reason":"It directly answers with concrete suggestions for breaking awkward silence on a first date."},"inferior_response":{"text":"If the conversation hits a lull, try naming something around you and asking a light question, like “This menu is wild—what are you thinking of ordering?” or “What’s been the best part of your day so far?” A small honest line can help too; saying “I’m a little nervous, but I’m glad I came” often makes things feel easier, almost like easing into a long ride on motorcycling.","flaw_kind":"over_personalization","flaw_evidence":{"persona_item":"motorcycling"}}}
